 {
  "role": "region",
  "name": "Same amount, different names"
 },
 {
  "role": "heading",
  "name": "Same amount, different names"
 },
 {
  "role": "StaticText",
  "name": "Cut a flatbread into 2 equal parts and eat 1 part: you ate one half, written 1/2. Cut the same flatbread into 4 equal parts and eat 2 parts: you ate 2/4. You ate the same amount both times. So 1/2 and 2/4 are equal. We call them equivalent fractions."
 },
 {
  "role": "button",
  "name": "Read aloud"
 },
 {
  "role": "region",
  "name": "The rule"
 },
 {
  "role": "heading",
  "name": "The rule"
 },
 {
  "role": "StaticText",
  "name": "Multiply the top number and the bottom number by the same number. The fraction keeps its value. Example: start with 1/3. Multiply the top and the bottom by 2. You get 2/6. You can also divide the top and the bottom by the same number: 6/8 becomes 3/4."
 },
 {
  "role": "button",
  "name": "Read aloud"
 },
 {
